    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct experimental absolute F measurement exists for the query molecule itself.",
    "L3 records are oral exposure measurements, not direct F determinations for the query.",
    "Structural differences from linezolid (5-chlorothiophene carboxamide, morpholin-3-one instead of morpholine, no fluorine) could alter absorption or first-pass, but no affirmative evidence indicates F <20%.",
    "Most non-linezolid/non-tedizolid L3 records are structurally distant or condition-specific; human fasted data for the exact query are absent.",
    "Food effect for the query is not assessed; the prediction is specifically for the fasted state."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Predicted high with high confidence: the query is a fasted-state oxazolidinone analog of linezolid, whose absolute oral bioavailability is consistently 93–103% in fasted humans; L3 oral exposure records for linezolid and tedizolid show substantial oral Cmax/AUC and high oral/IV exposure ratios, and no affirmative evidence supports F <20%."
}

